edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523906 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523906 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523565 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523906 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523906 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523906 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523906 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186523316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523906 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e6aac269-3443-59ce-abcc-30a3070cf5de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523914 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523914 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523914 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523914 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523914 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186523484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523914 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523914 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523914 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186523448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523914 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f80727cc-5fda-5d7f-a94d-a0834b4aa2eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523965 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523891 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523965 #edb/ref 1069 "q-184137" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523965 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523965 #edb/ref 1071 "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"Nine fewer than a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $p$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523965 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "71607034-c109-5c32-ac61-2615649524b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523965 #edb/ref 1074 "If we denote our number by $p,$ then the phrase \"nine fewer than a number\" can be written as \n\n$$\np-9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523969 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523969 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350260" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523969 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523969 #edb/ref 1071 "Olivia and Harper are musicians. In the previous season, the decimal proportion of Olivia’s performances that were solos was $0.55,$ while $40%$ of Harper’s performances were solos. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Less than half of Olivia's performances were solos.\n\nII. More than half of Harper's performances were solos.\n\nIII. Olivia had a greater percentage of solo performances compared to Harper." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523969 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "76598254-2f11-555f-8a0a-b51f61e7748b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523969 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n0.55>0.5,\n$$\n\nmore than half of Olivia's performances were solos.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n40%<50%.\n$$\n\nSo, less than half of Harper's performances were solos.\n\n- Statement III is true. We can compare $0.55$ and $40%$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.55\\times 100=55%\n$$\n\nSince $55%>40%,$ Olivia had a **greater** percentage of solo performances compared to Harper.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523979 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523979 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101924" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523979 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523979 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/72/72cfa1c8918f9f50b2426eb05ac16eed5605f557b59870aa914d07148d782676.png)\n\nA point $Q$ is shown on the axis above. To which quadrant does it belong?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523979 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "84a619bd-064d-5238-b773-07631be56d2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523979 #edb/ref 1074 "We label the quadrants as follows:\n\n![](images/0a/0a6e04eba0886d64c1a36b259c7a3c17afb9a86ad5169e28f476fff2d31c68b1.png)\n\nSince $Q$ is placed below and to the left of the origin, it lies in quadrant $\\text{III},$ which is the third quadrant." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523984 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523984 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128553" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523984 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523984 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following are natural numbers?\n\nI. $-1$\n\nII. $0$\n\nIII. $11$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523984 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ba50b21-9ef4-5151-a99b-e87a06229c81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523984 #edb/ref 1074 "The natural numbers consist of all positive whole numbers.\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5,…\n$$\n\nOf the given numbers, $11$ is a natural number, but $-1$ and $0$ are not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523991 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523991 #edb/ref 1069 "q-236833" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523991 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523991 #edb/ref 1071 "$23-48=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523991 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9d2a64c1-9bb3-5573-99a2-5c763e9021bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523991 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $48$ is larger than $23,$ the answer will be negative.\n\nWe start by solving an easier problem:\n\n$$\n48-23\n$$\n\nNext, we carry out the subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n48-23=25.\n$$\n\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. \n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n23-48=-25.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523999 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523999 #edb/ref 1069 "q-85400" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523999 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523999 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $9?$\n\nI. $7\\,050\\,113$\n\nII. $5\\,119\\,232$\n\nIII. $14\\,624\\,100$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523999 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a8e40c21-fa80-544c-8d3a-4f03c8add411" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186523999 #edb/ref 1074 "A number is divisible by $9$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $7\\,050\\,113$ is\n\n$$\n7+0+5+0+1+1+3=17,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $7\\,050\\,113$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $5\\,119\\,232$ is\n\n$$\n5+1+1+9+2+3+2=23,\n$$\n\nwhich is *not* divisible by $9.$ So, $5\\,119\\,232$ is *not* divisible by $9.$\n\n- The sum of the digits of $14\\,624\\,100$ is\n\n$$\n1+4+6+2+4+1+0+0=18,\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $9.$ So, $14\\,624\\,100$ is divisible by $9.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"llI only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524017 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523856 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524017 #edb/ref 1069 "q-59888" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524017 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524017 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/dd/dd9943f680dedd516084909e74d769e7605c7180f04d55b3c12113834bb47136.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of rectangles to the total number of shapes?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524017 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d65e17ea-2def-584a-904b-9397e33a3b17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524017 #edb/ref 1074 "We count the number of rectangles. We see that there are $3$ rectangles.\n\nWe count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $6$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of rectangles to total shapes is $3:6.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers in a ratio by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,3 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,6 &  \\\\ \\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,3 &  \\\\ \\,\\,1 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of rectangles to the total shapes is $1:2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524035 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186523848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524035 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128441" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524035 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524035 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $0÷(-\\frac{9}{7}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524035 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f162fba1-f09f-5af9-a84b-e3875292cc2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524035 #edb/ref 1074 "Zero divided by any number (other than zero) equals zero. Therefore, \n\n$$\n0÷(-\\frac{9}{7})=0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524042 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "07db862f-07ff-550f-b7db-a94183dc2e6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524042 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524048 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186524076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524048 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "315ebbfd-2ea0-5ceb-a85f-0680158355d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524048 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186523984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524051 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186524048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524051 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3962c57b-8223-5237-84cb-966ed91f92a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524051 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186523969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524069 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186524089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524069 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7310a483-c40f-5b26-a7a9-915a4dc0418c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186524069 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186523979 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
